paperweight-skel (0.2.85-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  Keybindings have changed:

    $mod+Return         terminal on the CURRENT workspace (used to switch
                        to workspace 1 first)
    $mod+Shift+Return   floating terminal on the current workspace
    $mod+t              terminal on workspace 1 (used to be the theme picker)
    $mod+Shift+t        floating terminal on workspace 1
    $mod+comma          NEW Settings menu: Theme, Wallpaper, Network, Sound,
                        Password setup, Power. Also opens with a right-click
                        on the PaperweightOS logo in the bar.

  The theme and wallpaper pickers no longer have their own keys ($mod+t,
  $mod+w). Open them from the Settings menu, or type "theme" or
  "wallpaper" into the app launcher ($mod+space).

  The upgrade updates ~/.config/sway for the installing user if those
  lines are still the stock ones. Customized configs are left alone; copy
  the new bindings from /etc/skel/.config/sway/config if you want them.
  Run `swaymsg reload` (or log out and back in) to apply.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0600
